One step is missing entirely. The notes say the tarball needs patching before it will build — and unpacking and patching is what prepare() is for. Add a prepare() function.

prepare() sits before build() in the order makepkg runs them. Give it a body that unpacks the source.

prepare() {
  tar -xf "$pkgname-$pkgver.tar.gz"
}

The four functions run in order: prepare, build, check, package. prepare() is where the source becomes a working tree — unpacked, patched, ready to compile — and skipping it is how a recipe ends up building the wrong thing.
